From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Ask whether the thread ceiling counts threads or bytes.

src/thread-probe settled what pthread_create itself can do. A bare title
creates 146 threads with exactly the attributes spawn_thread asks for --
1 MiB caller-supplied stack, system scope, no guard -- and sees EAGAIN
only once flexible memory is down to about a megabyte:

    A  wine's own: 1 MiB stack, system scope   created 146, flexible 1024K
    B  256 KiB stack, system scope             created 192 (cap), 7168K
    C  library's own stack (~16 MiB each)      created  28, flexible 0K
    H  after 2048 mprotect splits              created 141

So the mechanism is sound, the stack size is what sets the number, and VM
entries are not the resource -- H barely moved, and G showed munmap gives
every mapping back.

None of which fits this process, which is refused at a dozen threads with
146432K of flexible memory free, the same figure the alive tick has
reported unchanged in every run. Same errno, a different cause.

Two questions, asked where it is refused rather than guessed at from
outside: what flexible memory actually says at that instant, and whether a
256 KiB stack is accepted when a 1 MiB one is not. A retry that succeeds
means the ceiling is per-thread and size-shaped, and the 1 MiB kernel
stack is what to shrink. A retry refused means it counts threads, and no
stack size will help -- which would put the next look on what else this
process has that a bare title does not.

⚠ The retry's thread is pthread_exit itself, so it ends immediately, and it
is detached so nothing has to join it. One extra thread on the failure path
only.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
index 54d575ac81..672644b053 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -1404,9 +1404,43 @@ static NTSTATUS spawn_thread( struct thread_data *data )
      * STATUS_NO_MEMORY. Keep it, with the live thread count. Logged only on
      * failure: a working spawn costs nothing, and there are many now. */
     if (status)
-        ERR( "wine-ps5: spawn_thread tid=%04x FAILED pthread_create=%d threads=%d stack=%p+%zu\n",
+    {
+        /* ⚠ Ask the console two questions at the moment it refuses, because
+         * EAGAIN here does not mean what it means in a bare title.
+         *
+         * src/thread-probe creates 146 threads with exactly these attributes
+         * and only sees EAGAIN once flexible memory is down to about a
+         * megabyte -- yet this process is refused at a dozen with 143 MiB
+         * still free, which the alive tick has been reporting unchanged all
+         * along. Same errno, different cause.
+         *
+         * So: how much flexible memory there really is, and whether a much
+         * smaller stack is accepted. If the retry succeeds the ceiling is
+         * something per-thread and size-shaped, and Wine's 1 MiB kernel stack
+         * is the thing to shrink; if it is refused too, the ceiling counts
+         * threads and no stack size will help. */
+        extern int sceKernelAvailableFlexibleMemorySize( size_t *size );
+        size_t flexible = 0;
+        pthread_attr_t small;
+        pthread_t probe_id;
+        int retry;
+
+        if (sceKernelAvailableFlexibleMemorySize( &flexible )) flexible = 0;
+
+        pthread_attr_init( &small );
+        pthread_attr_setscope( &small, PTHREAD_SCOPE_SYSTEM );
+        pthread_attr_setstacksize( &small, 256 * 1024 );
+        retry = pthread_create( &probe_id, &small, (void * (*)(void *))pthread_exit, NULL );
+        pthread_attr_destroy( &small );
+        if (!retry) pthread_detach( probe_id );
+
+        ERR( "wine-ps5: spawn_thread tid=%04x FAILED pthread_create=%d threads=%d stack=%p+%zu "
+             "flexible=%zuK retry_256k=%d (%s)\n",
              (unsigned)data->tid, spawn_errno, (int)nb_threads, get_kernel_stack( data ),
-             (size_t)kernel_stack_size );
+             (size_t)kernel_stack_size, flexible >> 10, retry,
+             retry ? "a count, not a size: the stack is not what to shrink"
+                   : "a size: the 1 MiB kernel stack is what to shrink" );
+    }
 #endif
     pthread_attr_destroy( &attr );
     pthread_sigmask( SIG_SETMASK, &sigset, NULL );
